                <pb facs="0170" n="110" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg110"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2312.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The British minister and I have telegraphed
                    to our respective consuls at Kutien as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>It is most important that the persons arrested and executed are the real
                            culprits.</p></quote></p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
